  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Multisectoral Support to Enhance Integration of Refugees from Ukraine in Poland - 2024</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Building on the International Organization for Migration (IOM)&apos;s broad experience with implementing comprehensive shelter, protection, mental health and psychosocial support, and socio-economic inclusion programmes in Poland, the overall objective of this intervention is to address unpredictable and emerging needs of populations affected by the full-scale invasion of Ukraine in the medium to long-term. This programme has been designed in consideration of the dynamic nature of the conflict and the likelihood of displacement becoming protracted in the coming years. During this twelve-month project, IOM is supporting approximately 4,684 refugees, acknowledging the specific and intersectional vulnerabilities and needs of women, girls, boys, and men. In addition, IOM is engaging stakeholders operational in Poland with capacity building initiatives. Moreover, IOM continues to build evidence on information collected on mobility trends, vulnerabilities and needs to inform IOM and programming across humanitarian, development, peace nexus through the Displacement Tracking Matrix.</narrative>
  </description>
